ska2024 from the median-percent-change plot for the same reason as above.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/"]},{"current_value":"Inducer; Inhibitor","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"None","reason":"FDA labeling supports no clinically meaningful enzyme induction/inhibition; current filter contradicts the fact field.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"PR interval effect; QT prolongation","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"PR interval effect","reason":"FDA labeling states lacosamide did not prolong QTc and can increase PR interval.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; IV/IM injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Capsule; IV injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","reason":"FDA labeling supports IV injection only, not IM injection.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata FDA labeling; FDA/openFDA drug label API; NCBI LiverTox; NCBI Medical Genetics Summaries; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records","reason":"Replaces DailyMed/non-trusted list sources with trusted domains that support the retained facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547940/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK493589/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Makedonska2024","pmid":"38375995","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized 1:1 lacosamide/placebo, double-blind parallel-group pediatric focal-seizure trial; ClinicalTrials.gov record identifies NCT02477839 as Phase 3.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/"},{"label":"Vossler2020","pmid":"32817358","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; double-blind randomized placebo-controlled Phase 3 adjunctive trial for primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32817358/"},{"label":"Farkas2019","pmid":"31462582","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; double-blind randomized placebo-controlled pediatric focal-seizure trial; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01921205 identifies Phase 3.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/"},{"label":"FoldvarySchaefer2017","pmid":"28866338","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links with user approval; optionally retain only as a sleep/cognition tolerability reference elsewhere.","rationale":"PubMed identifies this as Clinical Trial, Phase IV. The endpoint was daytime sleepiness/noninferiority, not a phase II/III placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28866338/"},{"label":"Hong2016","pmid":"27669155","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized double-blind placebo-controlled Phase 3 adjunctive trial in Chinese and Japanese adults with partial-onset seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27669155/"},{"label":"Rudd2015","pmid":"25933358","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links with user approval; retain as cardiac-safety support if a separate safety-source field exists.","rationale":"This is a pooled cardiac safety analysis of clinical-trial data, not a primary phase II/III placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT report.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25933358/"},{"label":"Chung2010","pmid":"20132285","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized controlled adjunctive trial for partial-onset seizures with placebo arm and extractable 400 mg/day efficacy outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/"},{"label":"Halasz2009","pmid":"19183227","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized placebo-controlled adjunctive partial-onset seizure trial with extractable 400 mg/day outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/"},{"label":"BenMenachem2007","pmid":"17635557","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; multicenter double-blind placebo-controlled adult partial-onset seizure trial with extractable 400 mg/day outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","reason":"Mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; DailyMed wording should be avoided in source fields when trusted FDA/accessdata/openFDA sources are available.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label...","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_selected_current_fda_labeling; api_urls=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10 and https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA/openFDA/Drugs@FDA/accessdata, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 26/65 on 2026-05-15: 9 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 26 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Manual audit on 2026-05-20: retained Makedonska2024, Vossler2020, Farkas2019, Hong2016, Chung2010, Halasz2009, and BenMenachem2007 as qualifying lacosamide placebo-controlled phase II/III seizure-efficacy RCT reports. FoldvarySchaefer2017 is Phase IV sleepiness/cognition and Rudd2015 is pooled cardiac safety, so both require user approval before removal from the phase II/III RCT link field. Do not add Biton2015 as a missing RCT because it is a pooled safety/tolerability analysis of already represented trials, not an independent primary efficacy RCT.","reason":"Updates automated notes after manual concordance review.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28866338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25933358/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26414341/"]}],"summary":"Lacosamide row is mostly correct for identity, US availability, FDA approval year, indications, dosing, mechanism, half-life, metabolism, QT/PR facts, and RR50/seizure-freedom outcomes. Updates are needed for FDA boxed-warning sourcing, trusted evidence source names, alias completeness, contradictory enzyme/QT filters, IV-only formulation wording, two non-qualifying RCT links, and the median-percent-change field because Makedonska2024's 3.2% value is not a median percent-change differential."}
